{"post_stream": {"posts": [{"id": 266699, "name": "Simon Chen", "username": "simon17", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.auth0.com/simon17/{size}/33814_2.png", "created_at": "2023-03-19T18:52:23.462Z", "cooked": "<p>Hello, I\u2019m using the Resource Owner Password Flow to obtain an access token which I then use to access my API in e2e tests with Cypress. The issue is that the access token I get back does not contain an org_id since the Resource Owner Password Flow is not supported in the context of Organizations - however, our API requires the access token to contain an org_id, otherwise, the user  will not be allowed to access any endpoints. Is there a way to add an <code>org_id</code> to the access token returned from the Resource Owner Password Flow?</p>\n<p>I understand that I can utilize the Authorization Code Flow which utilizes the <code>/authorize</code> endpoint in order to add an org_id to the access token. However, this flow does not allow me to authenticate through a specific user. In this case, I need to receive an access token for a test user that I\u2019m using in the e2e tests but I also need the token to contain an org_id as well.</p>\n<p>Any help/advice is greatly appreciated!</p>", "post_number": 1, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-03-19T19:00:31.460Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 760, "reads": 36, "readers_count": 35, "score": 3807.2, "yours": false, "topic_id": 102885, "topic_slug": "add-org-id-to-access-token-returned-from-resource-owner-password-flow", "display_username": "Simon Chen", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 3, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 43338, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": false, "wiki": false, "post_url": "/t/add-org-id-to-access-token-returned-from-resource-owner-password-flow/102885/1", "user_signature": null, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true, "can_vote": false}, {"id": 266902, "name": "Ty", "username": "ty.frith", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.auth0.com/ty.frith/{size}/58484_2.png", "created_at": "2023-03-21T00:32:31.081Z", "cooked": "<p>Hello <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/simon17\">@simon17</a> welcome to the community!</p>\n<p>Unfortunately, as far I can tell this is not possible - Even if you temporarily disable organization for a specific application, and use the ROP flow + a rule to manually add a custom claim of <code>org_id</code>, you won\u2019t be able to as <code>org_id</code> is subject to <a href=\"https://auth0.com/docs/secure/tokens/json-web-tokens/create-custom-claims#general-restrictions\">restrictions</a>.</p>\n<p>The only option I can think of while using the ROP flow is to add a custom claim with an <code>org_id</code> but naming it something else, like <code>org_id1</code> - Obviously not ideal, but an option if you can work around this in testing.</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">function (user, context, callback) {\n\n    context.accessToken.org_id1 = \"your_org_id\";\n  \tcontext.idToken.org_id1 = \"your_org_id\";\n  \n  \treturn callback(null, user, context);\n\n}\n</code></pre>", "post_number": 3, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-03-21T00:32:31.081Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 10, "reads": 33, "readers_count": 32, "score": 61.6, "yours": false, "topic_id": 102885, "topic_slug": "add-org-id-to-access-token-returned-from-resource-owner-password-flow", "display_username": "Ty", "primary_group_name": "Auth0_Employees", "flair_name": "Auth0_Employees", "flair_url": "https://global.discourse-cdn.com/auth0/original/3X/d/c/dcd65ed8da0dd06e82c3ae1047aeab4c87f18097.jpeg", "flair_bg_color": "00000", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 41, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://auth0.com/docs/secure/tokens/json-web-tokens/create-custom-claims#general-restrictions", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Create Custom Claims", "clicks": 22}], "read": true, "user_title": "Community Engineer", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 36825, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": false, "wiki": false, "user_custom_fields": {"signature_cooked": "<p>If this post helped you, click the check mark <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/white_check_mark.png?v=15\" title=\":white_check_mark:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":white_check_mark:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> or give it a Like <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/+1.png?v=15\" title=\":+1:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":+1:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\">. When you do this, you\u2019re helping an entire community of developers just like you.</p>"}, "post_url": "/t/add-org-id-to-access-token-returned-from-resource-owner-password-flow/102885/3", "user_signature": "<p>If this post helped you, click the check mark <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/white_check_mark.png?v=15\" title=\":white_check_mark:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":white_check_mark:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> or give it a Like <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/+1.png?v=15\" title=\":+1:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":+1:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\">. When you do this, you\u2019re helping an entire community of developers just like you.</p>", "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 266975, "name": "Simon Chen", "username": "simon17", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.auth0.com/simon17/{size}/33814_2.png", "created_at": "2023-03-21T14:52:59.930Z", "cooked": "<p>Thanks for the reply <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/ty.frith\">@ty.frith</a> ! Do you know if the Auth0 team has any plans in the near future to enable the support of Organizations in the ROP flow? This would be a great feature to have when it comes to have.</p>", "post_number": 4, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-03-21T14:52:59.930Z", "reply_count": 1, "reply_to_post_number": 3, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 2, "reads": 29, "readers_count": 28, "score": 20.8, "yours": false, "topic_id": 102885, "topic_slug": "add-org-id-to-access-token-returned-from-resource-owner-password-flow", "display_username": "Simon Chen", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "reply_to_user": {"id": 36825, "username": "ty.frith", "name": "Ty", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.auth0.com/ty.frith/{size}/58484_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 43338, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 1, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": false, "wiki": false, "post_url": "/t/add-org-id-to-access-token-returned-from-resource-owner-password-flow/102885/4", "user_signature": null, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 266985, "name": "Ty", "username": "ty.frith", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.auth0.com/ty.frith/{size}/58484_2.png", "created_at": "2023-03-21T16:22:07.118Z", "cooked": "<p>Hey <a class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/simon17\">@simon17</a> no problem, I\u2019m happy to help where I can!</p>\n<p>ROPG support for organizations is on the radar (primarily for testing purposes similar to your needs), but there are no plans to support in the near future. I do however recommend creating a <a href=\"https://community.auth0.com/c/feedback/95\">feedback request</a> for this as I don\u2019t currently see anything related. It would be good to have it on record and the more votes it gets from community members the more likely it is to get attention.</p>", "post_number": 5, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-03-21T16:22:07.118Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": 4, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 6, "reads": 25, "readers_count": 24, "score": 35.0, "yours": false, "topic_id": 102885, "topic_slug": "add-org-id-to-access-token-returned-from-resource-owner-password-flow", "display_username": "Ty", "primary_group_name": "Auth0_Employees", "flair_name": "Auth0_Employees", "flair_url": "https://global.discourse-cdn.com/auth0/original/3X/d/c/dcd65ed8da0dd06e82c3ae1047aeab4c87f18097.jpeg", "flair_bg_color": "00000", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 41, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": "Community Engineer", "title_is_group": false, "reply_to_user": {"id": 43338, "username": "simon17", "name": "Simon Chen", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.auth0.com/simon17/{size}/33814_2.png"}, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": false, "admin": false, "staff": false, "user_id": 36825, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": false, "wiki": false, "user_custom_fields": {"signature_cooked": "<p>If this post helped you, click the check mark <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/white_check_mark.png?v=15\" title=\":white_check_mark:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":white_check_mark:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> or give it a Like <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/+1.png?v=15\" title=\":+1:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":+1:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\">. When you do this, you\u2019re helping an entire community of developers just like you.</p>"}, "post_url": "/t/add-org-id-to-access-token-returned-from-resource-owner-password-flow/102885/5", "user_signature": "<p>If this post helped you, click the check mark <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/white_check_mark.png?v=15\" title=\":white_check_mark:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":white_check_mark:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> or give it a Like <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/+1.png?v=15\" title=\":+1:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":+1:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\">. When you do this, you\u2019re helping an entire community of developers just like you.</p>", "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 269428, "name": "system", "username": "system", "avatar_template": "https://global.discourse-cdn.com/auth0/original/3X/b/5/b560f266932fcce5d57f09a6595bd50518cae3f3.jpeg", "created_at": "2023-04-04T16:23:28.112Z", "cooked": "<p>This topic was automatically closed 14 days after the last reply. New replies are no longer allowed.</p>", "post_number": 7, "post_type": 3, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2023-04-04T16:23:28.112Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 0, "reads": 22, "readers_count": 21, "score": 4.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 102885, "topic_slug": "add-org-id-to-access-token-returned-from-resource-owner-password-flow", "display_username": "system", "primary_group_name": null, "flair_name": null, "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": null, "flair_color": null, "flair_group_id": null, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "read": true, "user_title": null, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": true, "admin": true, "staff": true, "user_id": -1, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": false, "wiki": false, "action_code": "autoclosed.enabled", "post_url": "/t/add-org-id-to-access-token-returned-from-resource-owner-password-flow/102885/7", "user_signature": null, "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": false, "topic_accepted_answer": true}, {"id": 470414, "name": "Nikita Baleca", "username": "nik.baleca", "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/community.auth0.com/nik.baleca/{size}/68749_2.png", "created_at": "2026-02-25T18:00:15.494Z", "cooked": "<p>Hi everyone!</p>\n<p>In the context of performing automated tests in the context of organizations, it can be a difficult task since the usual <a href=\"https://auth0.com/docs/get-started/authentication-and-authorization-flow/resource-owner-password-flow\">ROPG grant flow</a> cannot be enabled.</p>\n<p>However, this can be resolved by using a <a href=\"https://auth0.com/docs/customize/actions/explore-triggers/signup-and-login-triggers/custom-token-exchange-trigger\">Custom Token Exchange Trigger</a> in which you will be able to set the organization as seen in this <a href=\"https://auth0.com/docs/customize/actions/explore-triggers/signup-and-login-triggers/custom-token-exchange-trigger/custom-token-exchange-api-object#api-authentication-setorganization-organization\">example</a>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"lang-auto\">exports.onExecuteCustomTokenExchange = async (event, api) =&gt; {\n\n  // 1. Validate subject_token\n  const subject_token = await validateToken(event.transaction.subject_token, jwksUri);\n\n  // 2.  Apply your authorization policy on the user\n  const isAuthorized = await authorizeAccess(subject_token.sub);\n  if (!isAuthorized) {\n    api.access.deny('Unauthorized_login', 'User cannot login due to reason: X');\n  }\n\n  // 3. Set the user for the transaction\n  api.authentication.setOrginzation('org_xS525r979AS33MSf');\n\n  // 4. Set the user for the transaction. You may also use setUserByConnection()\n  api.authentication.setUserById(subject_token.sub);\n\n  return;\n};\n</code></pre>\n<p>Hope this helps anybody who stumbles across the same issue!</p>\n<p>Kind Regards,<br>\nNik</p>", "post_number": 8, "post_type": 1, "posts_count": 5, "updated_at": "2026-02-25T18:00:15.494Z", "reply_count": 0, "reply_to_post_number": null, "quote_count": 0, "incoming_link_count": 2, "reads": 2, "readers_count": 1, "score": 10.4, "yours": false, "topic_id": 102885, "topic_slug": "add-org-id-to-access-token-returned-from-resource-owner-password-flow", "display_username": "Nikita Baleca", "primary_group_name": "DeveloperHubMembers", "flair_name": "DeveloperHubMembers", "flair_url": null, "flair_bg_color": "", "flair_color": "", "flair_group_id": 75, "badges_granted": [], "version": 1, "can_edit": false, "can_delete": false, "can_recover": false, "can_see_hidden_post": false, "can_wiki": false, "link_counts": [{"url": "https://auth0.com/docs/customize/actions/explore-triggers/signup-and-login-triggers/custom-token-exchange-trigger", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Custom Token Exchange Trigger - Auth0 Docs", "clicks": 0}, {"url": "https://auth0.com/docs/get-started/authentication-and-authorization-flow/resource-owner-password-flow", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Resource Owner Password Flow - Auth0 Docs", "clicks": 0}, {"url": "https://auth0.com/docs/customize/actions/explore-triggers/signup-and-login-triggers/custom-token-exchange-trigger/custom-token-exchange-api-object#api-authentication-setorganization-organization", "internal": false, "reflection": false, "title": "Actions Triggers: custom-token-exchange - API Object - Auth0 Docs", "clicks": 0}], "read": true, "user_title": "Auth0 Community Engineer", "title_is_group": false, "bookmarked": false, "actions_summary": [], "moderator": true, "admin": true, "staff": true, "user_id": 76022, "hidden": false, "trust_level": 4, "deleted_at": null, "user_deleted": false, "edit_reason": null, "can_view_edit_history": false, "wiki": false, "user_custom_fields": {"signature_cooked": "<p>If this post helped you, click the check mark <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/white_check_mark.png?v=15\" title=\":white_check_mark:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":white_check_mark:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> or give it a Like <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/+1.png?v=15\" title=\":+1:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":+1:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\">. When you do this, you\u2019re helping an entire community of developers just like you.</p>"}, "post_url": "/t/add-org-id-to-access-token-returned-from-resource-owner-password-flow/102885/8", "user_signature": "<p>If this post helped you, click the check mark <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/white_check_mark.png?v=15\" title=\":white_check_mark:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":white_check_mark:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> or give it a Like <img src=\"https://emoji.discourse-cdn.com/twitter/+1.png?v=15\" title=\":+1:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":+1:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\">. When you do this, you\u2019re helping an entire community of developers just like you.</p>", "can_accept_answer": false, "can_unaccept_answer": false, "accepted_answer": true, "topic_accepted_answer": true}], "strea